## Android SDK Platform-Tools: adb (bundled, unmodified)

- Project: Android SDK Platform-Tools by Google (the Android Open Source Project)
- Version: 37.0.1 (pinned in scripts/platform-tools.lock), from https://dl.google.com/android/repository/platform-tools-latest-windows.zip,
  SHA-256 45f4d63113e895ebde0c90f194099a4676b6ac653bd28d54314a9e022bbc1a99
- Shipped: `platform-toolsdb.exe`, `AdbWinApi.dll`, `AdbWinUsbApi.dll`, with Google's `NOTICE.txt` and `source.properties`
  (the other platform-tools programs are left out). Used only by the "Your Thor" card to install or update DS Forever over USB.
- Licences: adb is Android Open Source Project code under the Apache License 2.0; NOTICE.txt (shipped next to it) lists the
  licences of everything inside the platform-tools package. Google distributes the package under the Android SDK terms that
  apply to its download; projects such as scrcpy ship these same three files the same way.
- Desktop prefers an adb already on the PC's PATH (so it shares the adb server other tools use) and falls back to this one.

## Not bundled, needed for the controller

- ViGEmBus (Nefarius Software Solutions, BSD-3-Clause), the virtual gamepad driver Sunshine uses for the Thor's controller. It is
  a Windows kernel driver, so DS Forever Desktop does not install it; the user installs it from
  https://github.com/nefarius/ViGEmBus/releases if it is not already there.

## The DS Forever add-on set

- The add-ons in `companion\addons\` (with `companion\manifest.txt`) are DS Forever's own, the same set the Android app ships, under
  DS Forever's licence. They contain no Blizzard game files or art.

## World of Warcraft

- DS Forever Desktop ships no Blizzard files. It reads the game's own log (Logs/General.log) and Config.wtf on the user's PC, and
  writes only DS Forever's add-on folders under Interface/AddOns.
